================================================================================================
(1)  IS  W_hi + W_lo = (theta/2)<a,b>  AN IDENTITY?
================================================================================================
  a = lam_down(M_11);  b_k = lam_down_k(Y) + lam_down_{n+1-k}(Y).
  Generic M_11 and Y, no symmetry imposed on either.

     n       W_hi + W_lo    (theta/2)<a,b>    abs difference
  --------------------------------------------------------
     2    0.006017399391    0.006017399391          0.00e+00
     3    0.080062498263    0.080062498263          0.00e+00
     4   -0.142475353229   -0.142475353229          0.00e+00
     5   -0.095957351536   -0.095957351536          5.55e-17
     6    0.040849907485    0.040849907485          3.05e-16
     8   -0.015253952589   -0.015253952589          6.77e-17
    12    0.009536183631    0.009536183631          6.45e-16
    16   -0.064564404197   -0.064564404197          1.60e-15

  worst deviation over all n: 1.60e-15
  The endpoint sum is the inner product exactly, so symmetry of the
  interval IS the orthogonality <a,b> = 0 and nothing else.

